      "20260715": -0.08435109364533125,
      "20260814": -0.047686253606478525,
      "20260915": -0.027856898999595883
    },
    "negative_results": [
      "The Champion pool lost to equal weight on 3/3 dates. The sample is three signal dates, not a statistical test; no significance is claimed.",
      "SINGLE_FACTOR_MOMENTUM beat both the Champion and equal weight on 20260915 (+12.231% excess at h=5) and lost badly on 20260715 (-20.445% at h=10). One date winning does not make it a mechanism.",
      "INDUSTRY_NEUTRAL entered only 29 of 30 members on 20260715 before the round-robin key fix; after the fix it enters 30/30. The earlier 29/30 was caused by a stale pool, not by the limit-up exclusion.",
      "The 20260915 h=20 horizon never matured (cutoff is 20261016). It is reported as null and is NOT counted as zero."
    ],
    "known_module_defects_fixed_before_this_result": [
      "INDUSTRY_NEUTRAL keyed the round-robin by insertion order, so selectPool took preference ranks 31-60 instead of 1-30. Every INDUSTRY_NEUTRAL number in an earlier run was measuring a pool nobody designed. See test/ashare-experiment-a.test.mjs and the Phase 5 acceptance doc section 1.5."
    ],
    "eligibility_for_forward_observation": "NOT ELIGIBLE as a selection mechanism. The hypothesis under test was that the frozen ordering selects; it did not. Registering this as a candidate for shadow observation would spend forward capital on an ordering with no supporting evidence, and the pre-registered criterion is not met.",
